WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.247 --> 00:00:03.103
Please welcome Britt Lower!

2
00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:04.174
(audience applauds)

3
00:00:04.174 --> 00:00:06.100
Hi.

4
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.600
I'm so excited that you're here.

5
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:12.030
Adam Scott, your leading man, was just here,

6
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.600
and we were talking about the show.

7
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.850
I've been watching it.

8
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.620
It's insane, it is very different.

9
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:18.800
And I love that.

10
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.910
And I guess everybody else does too.

11
00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:21.790
That's what I'm hearing.

12
00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:26.600 line:15%
I mean, it's an office thriller with an odd sense of humor.

13
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.430
Okay, so is it true that you and your mom

14
00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:31.540
did face painting together?

15
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:32.490
It's true, yeah.

16
00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:35.393
And I actually, when I lived here in New York,

17
00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:38.030
just starting out as an actor,

18
00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:39.690
that's how I paid for my groceries.

19
00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.324
So I escaped being a starving artist

20
00:00:42.324 --> 00:00:44.793
by painting kids' faces.

21
00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:46.880
Wow, that's so cool.

22
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.210
Okay, something else we have in common

23
00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.170
that I'm really excited to ask you about is RVing.

24
00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:55.663
When I was 19, I discovered life on the road.

25
00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.453
But it's the most sort of liberating,

26
00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.440
I think it's the ultimate form of freedom.

27
00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.420
Why do you like it?

28
00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.510
Well, I think anytime I'm experiencing loss

29
00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:14.650
or heartbreak or need to heal, I like to get on the road,

30
00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:18.807
because it's this meditation of watching the miles go by.

31
00:01:18.807 --> 00:01:20.780
The other thing that I like to do with it

32
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.600
is I go and I find a small tenting circus

33
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.530
and I watch the circus,

34
00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.380 line:15%
and it's this sense of awe and wonderment.

35
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.630 line:15%
I mean, I just like to feel like I'm a kid again

36
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.890
and sit in the audience.

37
00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.290
Is it true that you also hopped in your RV, like you said,

38
00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.020
if you're having heartbreak or loss,

39
00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.250
like this is a breakup sort of cure-all for you.

40
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.083
Yeah.

41
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:43.700
Also, I saw something on your Instagram

42
00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.870
I wanted to pull up.
Okay.

43
00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:48.530
Is this due to a breakup response as well?

44
00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:50.310
You dyed your armpit hair blue.

45
00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.670
Yeah.

46
00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:55.260
You know, it's just like a little bit of subtle anarchy.

47
00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.230
Blue armpits.

48
00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:58.600
Yeah, I was going through a breakup.

49
00:01:58.600 --> 00:02:00.820
I mean, I've created total anarchy.

50
00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.510
One boyfriend was just a jerk

51
00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.810
and I went and spray painted his car

52
00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:07.060
in middle the night.
No.

53
00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.770
Oh yeah.
What color?

54
00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:11.570
I just used black and he called me the next day,

55
00:02:11.570 --> 00:02:12.930
and he's like, "Did you do this?"

56
00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:14.635
And I was like, "No."

57
00:02:14.635 --> 00:02:15.960
(audience laughs)

58
00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.420
But guess what?

59
00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:18.493
I did.

60
00:02:18.493 --> 00:02:19.326
(audience laughs)

61
00:02:19.326 --> 00:02:20.273
I'm impressed by you.

62
00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:23.070
That takes a lot to get the spray paint

63
00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:24.780
off of an automobile.

64
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.290
It was the funnest night too.

65
00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.590
We like blasted Cypress hill

66
00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:30.240
and did it in the middle of the night.

67
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.010
And I don't know, it just, the whole thing felt really good.

68
00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.540
I kind of wanna like spray paint something together.

69
00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.609
I kind of wanna have two people break up with us

70
00:02:38.609 --> 00:02:39.860
and see what you and I would do.

71
00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.130
We could Thelma and Louise it a little bit.

72
00:02:42.130 --> 00:02:43.083
What do you think?

73
00:02:43.083 --> 00:02:44.713
Yes!
You and me.

74
00:02:44.713 --> 00:02:48.527
(audience applauds)

75
00:02:48.527 --> 00:02:50.944
So tell us about "Severance."

76
00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.930
It's a really interesting show.

77
00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.840
It's very avant garde, very unique.

78
00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.680
It's really popular with people right now.

79
00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:04.790
And is it true that, I wanted to relate to you again,

80
00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:07.540
that you work in a windowless room in it?

81
00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:12.250
'Cause we don't see the daylight here ever.

82
00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:15.630
Yeah, so the office is built in this way

83
00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.030 line:15%
to make you feel a certain way.

84
00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.630 line:15%
And the audience, you know, it takes you on this journey

85
00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.493 line:15%
of yeah, it's windowless, fluorescent lighting.

86
00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.690
We were all going a little bonkers wearing masks

87
00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:29.930
and shields, no windows.

88
00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.220
And all of a sudden one day,

89
00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.760
someone left the outside door open.

90
00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.330
We were filming in the Bronx.

91
00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:40.240
And a very friendly chicken walked on to our sound stage,

92
00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:42.840
out of nowhere, starts making itself at home.

93
00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.370
It's like sitting on the sound booth,

94
00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.369
they're feeding it strawberries.

95
00:03:46.369 --> 00:03:50.480
It goes outside and someone's holding an umbrella.

96
00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:52.440
Oh my god, that's the chicken?

97
00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:53.273
That's the chicken.

98
00:03:53.273 --> 00:03:56.387
I have six chickens, I gotta say, that is a real looker.

99
00:03:56.387 --> 00:03:57.220
(audience laughs)

100
00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:59.400
And so, look, it's sitting on someone's shoulder.

101
00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:00.445
Look, this is-
Oh my god.

102
00:04:00.445 --> 00:04:02.860
I love that someone's holding the umbrella.

103
00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.320
We all became so endeared by this chicken

104
00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:09.130
who had just arrived, this random arrival of a chicken

105
00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:10.310
at our sound stage.

106
00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:11.890
And it brought everyone so much joy.

107
00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.700
You could see their smile above their masks.

108
00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:17.400
And it was the perfect metaphor for this show

109
00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:19.950
where a lot of bizarre things happen in "Severance."

110
00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:23.070
And I think that the art meets life of it all.

111
00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.510
We all kind of came to work to like,

112
00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:28.460
ooh, what kind of weird, odd thing might happen on our set.

113
00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:31.210 line:15%
And much like the circus, little odd moments

114
00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:34.920 line:15%
or just to see like the beauty in a moment like that,

115
00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:37.690 line:15%
to be moved from it, you know?

116
00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.080
I mean, I would be so thrilled

117
00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.720
if a chicken came through this set.

118
00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.256
Actually, my best friend Chicken is here somewhere.

119
00:04:44.256 --> 00:04:47.949
(audience applauds)

120
00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:51.007
Britt Lower, I'm so honored that you've come on our show.

121
00:04:51.007 --> 00:04:53.890
"Severance" is streaming now on Apple TV+,

122
00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:56.950
with new episodes dropping every Friday.

123
00:04:56.950 --> 00:05:00.117 line:15%
(upbeat bright music)

